          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "कपालम् (kapālam) is traced to the root √kamp in the Uṇādi list that MW follows; its first senses are \"a cup, a dish\", and \"the skull, the cranium\" comes after them (MW)."
